<td id="S3.T1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="S3.SS3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4(N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}})D{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}(\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Enc</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Dec</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" mathsize="0.900em">S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4(N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}})D{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}(\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S3.T1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="S3.SS3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24(N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}})LD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Enc</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Dec</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24(N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}})LD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Table 1: </span>Forward-pass training FLOPs comparison.
<math id="S3.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of layers, <math id="S3.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> the sequence length, <math id="S3.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> the block size, and <math id="S3.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> the hidden dimension.
The expression highlighted in <span id="S3.T1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">blue</span> denotes the number of attention operations.
E2D2 refers to block diffusion parameterization.
For E2D2, we separate <math id="S3.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S3.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{Enc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{Enc}}</annotation></semantics></math> encoder and <math id="S3.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{Dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{Dec}}</annotation></semantics></math> decoder layers.
We provide the derivation in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Training FLOPs derivation ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.
</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
