<td id="S3.T2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">AR</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.SS3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\cdot O(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\cdot O(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S3.T2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">MDLM</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S3.SS3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\cdot O(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\cdot O(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S3.T2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">BD3LM</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.SS3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BT\cdot O(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BT\cdot O(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S3.T2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">E2D2</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S3.SS3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{B\cdot O(\phi)}_{\text{encoder}}+\underbrace{BT\cdot O(\theta)}_{\text{decoder}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext mathsize="0.900em">encoder</mtext></munder><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext mathsize="0.900em">decoder</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{B\cdot O(\phi)}_{\text{encoder}}+\underbrace{BT\cdot O(\theta)}_{\text{decoder}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Table 2: </span>Inference FLOPs comparison.
<math id="S3.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is cost of a decoder call and <math id="S3.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is cost of an encoder call.
For E2D2, <math id="S3.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\theta)\ll O(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\theta)\ll O(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S3.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> denotes diffusion steps and <math id="S3.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> the number of blocks.
E2D2 uses the block diffusion parameterization.
</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Training Algorithm</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we review the algorithm and complexity of a forward pass through the E2D2 model to compute the loss of the block diffusion objective. The training procedure for E2D2 is presented in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.4 Training Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
We model the posterior probabilities <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}_{s}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{C})</annotation></semantics></math> for all blocks <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in[1,\dots,B]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in[1,\dots,B]</annotation></semantics></math> and context tokens <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of their position indices.
For block diffusion, context tokens for block <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to previous clean blocks <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{C}={\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{C}={\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Naively, we would compute logits by invoking the encoder and decoder for each block in a loop, since the logits for each block are conditioned on block-specific inputs <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. This entails calling the encoder <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}_{t}^{C}=\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Encoder</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}_{t}^{C}=\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{C})</annotation></semantics></math> to encode the conditioning <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and the decoder to compute <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{b}=\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{h}}_{t}^{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>logit</mtext><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Decoder</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{b}=\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{h}}_{t}^{C})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vectorized Implementation</span> 
To efficiently model all posterior probabilities across <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> blocks using a single encoder and decoder pass, we process all clean tokens <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> through the encoder and noised tokens <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> through the decoder. We design custom attention masks (Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.4 Training Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) to ensure that noisy tokens attend within their noised block and to previous clean blocks, inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_figure ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:179.4pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Encoder-Decoder Training</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">datapoint </span><math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, noise process </span><math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><span id="alg2.l1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Encoder</span><span id="alg2.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> w/ params. </span><math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><span id="alg2.l1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Decoder</span><span id="alg2.l1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> w/ params. </span><math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, diffusion loss </span><math id="alg2.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">repeat</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Sample </span><math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}\sim q_{t}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}\sim q_{t}(\cdot|{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}\leftarrow\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐡</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Encoder</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℳ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Enc</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}\leftarrow\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{1:L}\leftarrow\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L},{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">logit</mtext><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Decoder</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐡</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℳ</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Dec</mtext></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{1:L}\leftarrow\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L},{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  Take gradient step on </span><math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta,\phi}\mathcal{L}({\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{1:L};\theta,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∇</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">logit</mtext><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta,\phi}\mathcal{L}({\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{1:L};\theta,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">until</span><span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> converged
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, the clean sequence <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> is passed to the encoder with a block-causal mask <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce the representations <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> so that each clean block is conditioned on itself <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math> and previous blocks <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}</annotation></semantics></math>(Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.4 Training Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, left).
In the decoder, for a given noisy block <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, each token attends to tokens within its block <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math> and clean token representations from preceding blocks <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we denote as <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}^{&lt;b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}^{&lt;b}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The decoder attention mechanism operates over <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2L</annotation></semantics></math> keys and values corresponding to the <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens in <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens in <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}.</annotation></semantics></math>
The decoder attention pattern is enforced through an attention mask <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times 2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times 2L}</annotation></semantics></math> (Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.4 Training Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, right).
We thus perform an encoder pass over the entire clean sequence, followed by a decoder pass over the entire noisy sequence, as follows:
<math id="S3.SS4.p3.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}=\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Encoder</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L}=\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p3.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{1:L}=\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L},{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Decoder</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐡</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{logit}}^{1:L}=\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L},{\mathbf{h}}^{1:L},\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, using a smaller decoder significantly improves training throughput relative to a decoder-only BD3LM model.
In Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.3 Sampling Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we depict the FLOPs comparison between modeling paradigms and E2D2 applied to block diffusion, see Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Training FLOPs derivation ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> for a detailed derivation.
Letting <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be the total number of layers in the model, which for E2D2 we have <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that for same number of layers, E2D2 uses <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math> fewer FLOPs compared to BD3LM.
Moreover, for any block diffusion model of block size <math id="S3.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S&lt;L," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S&lt;L,</annotation></semantics></math> we achieve fewer training FLOPs relative to standard masked diffusion models (MDLM; see Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C FLOPs comparison to MDLM ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>) while maintaining the superior quality of the BD3LM block diffusion parameterization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="99.39" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 484.45 99.39" width="484.45"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,99.39) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(42.41,0) translate(0,-51.61)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(0.29 0.0 0.0 0.29 -41.07 141.36)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.65em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:29.8pt;" height="28.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 28.64)" width="439.3"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S3.F2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:298%;">Encoder Attn. Mask<span id="S3.F2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="S3.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{enc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>enc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{enc}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#87CEFA;--ltx-fill-color:#87CEFA;--ltx-fg-color:#87CEFA;" color="#87CEFA" fill="#87CEFA" stroke="#87CEFA"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 125.59 M 0 125.59 L 0 137 L 11.42 137 L 11.42 125.59 Z M 11.42 137"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#87CEFA;--ltx-fill-color:#87CEFA;--ltx-fg-color:#87CEFA;" color="#87CEFA" fill="#87CEFA" stroke="#87CEFA"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 11.42 125.59 M 11.42 125.59 L 11.42 137 L 22.83 137 L 22.83 125.59 Z M 22.83 137"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path style="stro