<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Table 3: </span>CNN/DailyMail test set ROUGE scores.
Best values for our trained models are <span id="S4.T3.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded.</span>
<math id="S4.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> refers to number of transformer layers (<math id="S4.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{Enc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{Enc}}</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="S4.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{Dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{Dec}}</annotation></semantics></math> for E2D2).
Decoding throughput (<span id="S4.T3.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tput</span>) is measured in tokens / sec on 1 <span id="S4.T3.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">H100 80GB</span> machine.
For all models, we use <math id="S4.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=L</annotation></semantics></math> sampling steps, so the throughput can be higher for diffusion when <math id="S4.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&lt;L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&lt;L</annotation></semantics></math>.
We report mean <math id="S4.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> standard deviation for 100 samples.
</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
