<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A7.SS2" title="In Appendix G Generated Samples ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">G.2 </span>BD3LM (<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=21</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></nav>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Extended Background on Block Diffusion Language Models</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we provide an extended overview of block diffusion language models closely following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>.
In particular, we define the masking process <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}^{1:B}_{t}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{1:B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}^{1:B}_{t}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{1:B})</annotation></semantics></math> and the derivation of the objective <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:B};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:B};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> for parameters <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we factorize the sequence <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from the data distribution <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\mathbf{x}}^{1:L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{x}}^{1:L})</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> blocks of size <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.
We simplify notation by denoting the tokens <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{(b-1)\cdot S:b\cdot S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{(b-1)\cdot S:b\cdot S}</annotation></semantics></math> in a block <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We perform diffusion in each block over <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> discretization steps.
We define <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,s</annotation></semantics></math> to denote <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)=i/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)=i/T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(i)=(i-1)/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(i)=(i-1)/T</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,T]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We denote the Kullback-Leibler divergence as <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Below we reproduce the negative evidence lower bound (NELBO) following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(1):t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\prod_{i=1}^{T}{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s(i)}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(i)},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{\prod_{i=1}^{T}q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(i)}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s(i)})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\sum_{b=1}^{B}\log\mathbb{E}_{q}\frac{{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(T)}|{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\prod_{i=1}^{T}{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s(i)}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(i)},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}{\prod_{i=1}^{T}q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t(i)}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s(i)})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{b=1}^{B}\bigg[\underbrace{-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>recons</mtext></msub></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{b=1}^{B}\bigg[\underbrace{-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{2}{T},\dots,\frac{T-1}{T},1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>D</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{t\in\left\{\frac{2}{T},\dots,\frac{T-1}{T},1\right\}}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}}\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>D</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub></munder><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 40.00006pt+\underbrace{\text{D}_{KL}\left(q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)}_{\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}}\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Forward Noise Process</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within each block, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> adopt the masked diffusion language modeling framework, which is the most performant <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
They use a simplified NELBO as proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, we first define a diffusion matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times V}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to noise level <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for states <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,V\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,V\}</annotation></semantics></math> and vocabulary size <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that the prior distribution is the absorbing mask state <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a one-hot vector centered on the special <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">[MASK]</span> token index.
We denote this mask index as the last token in the vocabulary, <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmax_{i}{\mathbf{m}}_{i}=V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmax_{i}{\mathbf{m}}_{i}=V</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the noise schedule function <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is monotonically decreasing in <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the diffusion matrix is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[Q_{t}]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }i=j=V\\
\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }i=j\neq V\\
1-\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }j=V,i\neq V\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[Q_{t}]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if }i=j=V\\
\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }i=j\neq V\\
1-\alpha_{t}&amp;\text{if }j=V,i\neq V\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the forward marginal <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t|s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t|s}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use forward marginal probabilities according to <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t|s}=\alpha_{t}/\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t|s}=\alpha_{t}/\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The forward noise process is applied independently for each token <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,\dots L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,\dots L\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first define the transition matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Q}_{t(i)}=Q_{t(1)}Q_{t(2)}\dots Q_{t(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Q}_{t(i)}=Q_{t(1)}Q_{t(2)}\dots Q_{t(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> which is used in the forward process <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t};\overline{Q}_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t};\overline{Q}_{t}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Reverse Denoising Process</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now may obtain the reverse posterior <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> derived in D3PM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> as follows, where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\odot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\odot</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Hadamard product between two vectors:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}{q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}{{({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t})}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Cat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})=\frac{q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s},{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}{q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell})}=\text{Cat}\left({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s};\frac{Q_{t|s}{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\odot Q_{s}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}{{({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t})}^{\top}Q_{t}^{\top}{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Negative Evidence Lower Bound (NELBO)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As in block diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, we adopt the simplified objective for masked diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> to obtain a tighter NELBO. We provide the sketch for the derivation, with the full proof is provided in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first focus on simplifying the diffusion loss term in (<a href="#A1.Ex1" title="In Appendix A Extended Background on Block Diffusion Language Models ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
To simplify the denoising model, we enforce the following constraints on the design of the denoising network by taking advantage of the fact that there only exists two possible states in the diffusion process <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\in\{{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell},{\mathbf{m}}\}\;\forall\ell\in\{1,\dots,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\in\{{\mathbf{x}}^{\ell},{\mathbf{m}}\}\;\forall\ell\in\{1,\dots,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Zero Masking Probabilities</span>. The clean sequence does not contain masks. So, we set <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}={\mathbf{m}}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}={\mathbf{m}}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Carry-Over Unmasking</span>. If a token is unmasked in the reverse denoising process, it is never remasked by definition of the masked diffusion process.
The true reverse posterior for the case where <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we set <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}\neq{\mathbf{m}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With these two simplifications, we now use our denoising model to parameterize the posterior <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{s}={\mathbf{x}}^{\ell}|{\mathbf{z}}^{\ell}_{t}={\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a token in the <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-th position in block <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\{1,\dots,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\{1,\dots,B\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The diffusion loss term is derived as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left[q({\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell})\|{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{s}|{\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A1.Ex8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{D}_{\text{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext mathsize="0.800em">D</mtext><mtext mathsize="0.800em">KL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{D}_{\text{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.Ex8.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> is simply the discrete-time diffusion loss for the block <math id="A1.Ex8.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>; hence, from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> (Suppl. B.1), we get:</span></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{L^{\prime}}\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b,\ell}\mid{\mathbf{z}}^{b,\ell}_{t},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t}\mathbb{E}_{q}T\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, we obtain a tighter approximation of the likelihood by taking the diffusion steps <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>, for which <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})=\alpha_{t}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(\alpha_{t}-\alpha_{s})=\alpha_{t}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">When taking <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> (Suppl. A.2.4) show the reconstruction loss becomes 0. In particular, we use the fact that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t(1)}^{b}\sim\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\text{Cat}\left(.;{\mathbf{z}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b}\right)=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{x}}^{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t(1)}^{b}\sim\lim_{T\rightarrow\infty}\text{Cat}\left(.;{\mathbf{z}}_{t=\frac{1}{T}}^{b}\right)=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{x}}^{b})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>recons</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{recons}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(1)}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{q}\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(1)}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(1)}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}|{\mathbf{z}}_{t(1)}^{b}={\mathbf{x}}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Also, the prior loss <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}=\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left(q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>prior</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext>D</mtext><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{prior}}=\text{D}_{\text{KL}}\left(q({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})\parallel{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}^{b}_{t=1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to 0 since <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t=1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t=1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\mathbf{z}}_{t=1}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{z}}_{t=1}^{b}|{\mathbf{x}}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{t=1}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>Cat</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{p_{\theta}}({\mathbf{z}}_{t=1}^{b})=\text{Cat}(.;{\mathbf{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> (Suppl. A.2.4).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The final diffusion objective simply becomes a weighted average of cross-entropy terms:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{BD}}({\mathbf{x}};\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{BD}}({\mathbf{x}};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{b=1}^{B}\mathbb{E}_{t\sim[0,1]}\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\frac{\alpha_{t}^{\prime}}{1-\alpha_{t}}\log p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{b}\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{b},{\mathbf{x}}^{&lt;b})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Training FLOPs derivation</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the training FLOPs of a model forward pass in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.3 Sampling Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> as follows.
Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> be the sequence length, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of layers, and <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be the hidden dimension.
We calculate the attention FLOPs of the forward pass following FlashAttention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, which is <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4NDL^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4NDL^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for bidirectional attention, as each matrix multiplication (i.e., multiplying queries and keys and multiplying the attention output by values) requires <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2NDL^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2NDL^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Assuming a gated MLP with three dense layers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> and intermediate hidden dimension of <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4D</annotation></semantics></math>, the MLP FLOPs are given as <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24NLD^{2}=2NL(D)(4D)\text{ (up-projection) }+2NL(D)(4D)\text{ (gate projection) }+2NL(4D)(D)\text{ (down-projection)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (up-projection) </mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (gate projection) </mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (down-projection)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24NLD^{2}=2NL(D)(4D)\text{ (up-projection) }+2NL(D)(4D)\text{ (gate projection) }+2NL(4D)(D)\text{ (down-projection)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Autoregressive.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The number of attention operations in causal attention is: <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{L}i=\frac{L^{2}+L}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{L}i=\frac{L^{2}+L}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, AR training uses <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4ND(\frac{L^{2}+L}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4ND(\frac{L^{2}+L}{2})</annotation></semantics></math> attention FLOPs. The MLP FLOPs are given as <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24NLD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24NLD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Full-Sequence Diffusion.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sequence diffusion models such as Masked Diffusion LMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> training uses <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4NDL^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4NDL^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> attention FLOPs from bidirectional attention, requiring <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> attention operations. The MLP FLOPs are also <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24NLD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24NLD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Block Diffusion.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For block diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, the sequence is split into <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> blocks of size <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=BS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=BS</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The training algorithm proposed in BD3LM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math> more computationally expensive relative to both AR and full-sequence diffusion.
Below, we summarize the attention operations used to compute the attention FLOPs from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">BD3LM uses attention mask <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD3LM}}\in\{0,1\}^{2L\times 2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD3LM</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD3LM}}\in\{0,1\}^{2L\times 2L}</annotation></semantics></math> for both the noised tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and clean tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This mask can visualized as a concatenation of the encoder and decoder masks from Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.4 Training Algorithm ‣ 3 Efficient Encoder-Decoder Diffusion ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
This mask is thus comprised of four <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\times L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\times L</annotation></semantics></math> smaller attention masks:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD3LM}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}\\
\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}\\
\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD3LM</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>OBC</mtext></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD3LM}}=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{0}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}\\
\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}&amp;\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}\\
\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>OBC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}</annotation></semantics></math> are used to update the representation of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> is used to update the representation of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define these masks as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Block-causal self-attention mask</span> to update clean <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:B}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{M}_{BC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in the same block as $i$, or a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mtext> belongs in the same block as </mtext><mi>i</mi><mtext>, or a block before </mtext><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{M}_{BC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in the same block as $i$, or a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero for <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{b=1}^{B}bS^{2}=\frac{S^{2}B^{2}+BS^{2}}{2}=\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{b=1}^{B}bS^{2}=\frac{S^{2}B^{2}+BS^{2}}{2}=\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> entries</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Block-diagonal self-attention mask</span> to update noised <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:B}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{M}_{BD}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $i,j$ are in the same block}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext> are in the same block</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{M}_{BD}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $i,j$ are in the same block}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero for <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BS^{2}=LS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BS^{2}=LS</annotation></semantics></math> entries.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Offset block-causal cross-attention mask</span> to update <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:B}</annotation></semantics></math> via cross-attention to <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:B}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{M}_{OBC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mi>j</mi><mtext> belongs in a block before </mtext><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{M}_{OBC}\right]_{ij}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\text{if $j$ belongs in a block before $i$}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}=\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}-\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>OBC</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}=\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}-\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the number of nonzero entries is <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}-LS=\frac{L^{2}-LS}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}-LS=\frac{L^{2}-LS}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the total number of attention operations is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}+LS+\frac{L^{2}-LS}{2}=L^{2}+LS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}+LS+\frac{L^{2}-LS}{2}=L^{2}+LS</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The number of MLP FLOPs is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48NLD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48NLD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as the input sequence to each layer is of length <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2L</annotation></semantics></math> from both <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}^{1:L}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Encoder-Decoder Block Diffusion (Ours).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">E2D2 uses half the attention FLOPs compared to BD3LM by splitting the operation into encoder and decoder layers.
This is because each encoder and decoder layer uses the same number of attention FLOPs.</p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Encoder attention operations</span>. The encoder uses mask <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}=\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BC</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{Enc}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times L}=\mathcal{M}_{\text{BC}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the encoder uses <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> attention operations</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Decoder attention operations</span>. The decoder uses mask <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times 2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{Dec}}\in\{0,1\}^{L\times 2L}</annotation></semantics></math> = <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}\oplus\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>OBC</mtext></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>BD</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{OBC}}\oplus\mathcal{M}_{\text{BD}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the decoder uses <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{L^{2}-LS}{2}+LS=\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{L^{2}-LS}{2}+LS=\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> attention operations.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The FLOPs of an attention pass is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4(N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}})D\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4(N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}})D\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The MLP FLOPs is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24NLD^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24NLD^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> since the input sequence contains <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens at each layer.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>FLOPs comparison to MDLM</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we show that E2D2 attention FLOPs for the block diffusion parameterization are upper-bounded by decoder-only MDLM FLOPs under the same model size. Assume both models have the same number of total layers, where <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Enc</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>Dec</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=N_{\text{Enc}}+N_{\text{Dec}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{FLOPs}_{\text{E2D2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>E2D2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{FLOPs}_{\text{E2D2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MDLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mtext>FLOPs</mtext><mtext>MDLM</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\text{FLOPs}_{\text{MDLM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 4ND\left(\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 4ND\left(\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4NDL^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4NDL^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{L^{2}+LS}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{L+S}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{L+S}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">So, as long as <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S&lt;L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S&lt;L</annotation></semantics></math>, E2D2 FLOPs are fewer than that of MDLM under equal model size.
When <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=L</annotation></semantics></math>, we exactly recover MDLM FLOPs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>MDLM with Encoder-Decoder Architecture</h2>

<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> prompt tokens.
We denote the set of unmasked token indices in <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=\{\ell\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\ell}\neq{\mathbf{m}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=\{\ell\mid{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\ell}\neq{\mathbf{m}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we define <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{C_{t}}=\bigoplus_{\ell\in C_{t}}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{C_{t}}=\bigoplus_{\ell\in C_{t}}{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The encoder receives inputs <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t,\text{Enc}}={\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}\oplus{\mathbf{x}}^{C_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>Enc</mtext></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t,\text{Enc}}={\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}\oplus{\mathbf{x}}^{C_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and produces representations <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampling</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ Sampling ‣ Appendix D MDLM with Encoder-Decoder Architecture ‣ Encoder-Decoder Diffusion Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we present the sampling procedure for MDLM parameterized by an encoder-decoder architecture.
We denote the denoising steps budget as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, and the reverse diffusion process proceeds as <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\frac{T-1}{T}\ldots,\frac{1}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\frac{T-1}{T}\ldots,\frac{1}{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also denote the number of steps where only the decoder is called by <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the encoder will be invoked at time steps <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\frac{T-n}{T},\frac{T-2n}{T},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\frac{T-n}{T},\frac{T-2n}{T},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by encoding the <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> prompt tokens <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}</annotation></semantics></math> to attain the encoder representation <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}^{1:P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}^{1:P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The decoder’s input is initialized to a sequence of length <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of only masked tokens.
The decoder iteratively denoises this full sequence for a fixed number of steps <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with cross-attention to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}_{1}={\mathbf{h}}^{1:P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐡</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}_{1}={\mathbf{h}}^{1:P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Later in the decoding process, in some interval <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=t-\frac{n}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=t-\frac{n}{T}</annotation></semantics></math>), during which only the decoder is invoked over <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> evaluations and the encoder is not invoked, we treat <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> as constant for all <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math>.
At <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, the decoder returns any new tokens decoded from the interval <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math>, which are incorporated into the encoder’s input, and the encoder is evaluated to produce an updated <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This process is repeated until the sampling budget <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is exhausted.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<div id="alg3.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt </span><math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{1:P}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, number of steps during which only the decoder is invoked </span><math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, number diffusion steps </span><math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><span id="alg3.l1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Encoder</span><span id="alg3.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><span id="alg3.l1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Decoder</span><span id="alg3.l1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, algorithm </span><span id="alg3.l1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">Sample</span><span id="alg3.l1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{h}}\leftarrow\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐡</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Encoder</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{h}}\leftarrow\textsc{Encoder}({\mathbf{x}}^{1:P})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg3.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Encode prompt
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}\sim{\mathbf{m}}^{1:L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐦</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}\sim{\mathbf{m}}^{1:L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg3.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize fully noised sequence
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg3.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=T,T-n,T-2n,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=T,T-n,T-2n,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg3.l4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg3.l4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow\frac{i}{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow\frac{i}{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span><span id="alg3.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="alg3.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> steps </span><span id="alg3.l6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">do</span><span id="alg3.l6.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}\leftarrow\textsc{Sample}(\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L},{\mathbf{h}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Sample</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Decoder</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐡</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L}\leftarrow\textsc{Sample}(\textsc{Decoder}({\mathbf{z}}_{t}^{1:L},{\mathbf{h}}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg3.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="alg3.l7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg3.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Denoise sequence: Apply small decoder only
</span>
</div>
